From ecb2b7bf95e476b7964c37a4432b07043ac4bdf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 10:07:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06880/11362] [outer-loop] wire live behavioral mechanic-class
 inference into E3AgentPolicy

Closes the gap operator identified: "make sure we have that wiring in the
live agent" for genre/rule-kind inference to prioritize moves, not
per-game memorization.

arc_solve_learning.extract_early_play_signature() and
classify_early_play_mechanic() already existed and were already reachable
from the live import closure, but the scored E3AgentPolicy never fed them
a real early_play_signature -- _feature_router_payload always returned
enabled=False, reason=early_play_signature_not_supplied in practice. This
was pure behavioral dead code: click/keyboard effect density, avatar
motion detection, cell-connect detection, hidden-carry-state detection,
and config-toggle detection, computed with zero game-identity lookup and
zero use of the executable win-check.

New: _early_play_rows() converts E3AgentPolicy.transitions (this game's
OWN observed transitions, real hidden games included) into the row shape
the classifier expects. _maybe_route_from_transitions() fires once per
game after 8 transitions accumulate (matching
extract_early_play_signature's own k), classifies the behavioral
signature, and -- above a confidence floor -- biases
uses_goal_distance_heuristic (and the derived explore budget), mirroring
the existing _maybe_route_from_frame precedent. self.feature_router is
always populated for observability even below the confidence floor.

Deliberately conservative: results/experiment_4582_feature_router_
transfer.json already measured the closely-related idea of switching the
entire offline solver by classified mechanic and found no value
(transfer_delta=0.0, did not beat a random-route control). What's wired
here is narrower -- it never swaps solvers, only adjusts one existing
budget-sizing flag inside the same E3AgentPolicy cascade -- but inherits
the same classifier, so it's gated behind
_FEATURE_ROUTER_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.5 and treated as provisional until it
has its own controlled measurement, not assumed to move the scored win
rate.

Verified: scripts/arc_orphan_solver_lint.py passes (49 live-reachable
modules), live end-to-end smoke test against the offline arcade (tn36,
real transitions, no crashes, correct classification + confidence-gate
suppression), full existing arc_competition_agent/arc_solve_learning test
suite still green (54 passed pre-existing + 3 pre-existing unrelated
failures reproduced identically on unmodified HEAD), new 7-test
regression file (tests/python/test_experiment_4582_live_feature_router_
wiring.py) covers row conversion, once-per-game firing, game-identity
independence, and both sides of the confidence gate.

